{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_h3567akgalkwytjqyaelsbj4ev4xwlh3oedzzzmbsd3a2dkuqyva","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — the Rust translation matches the C byte-for-byte.** No Rust source changes were needed; the translation was already correct. The real findings were in the test harness.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — symbol parity | ✅ `driver` is the only export in both; symbol diff **empty**; 0 missing non-libc undefined symbols |\n| Phase B — every `CONFIGS.md` row (13) | ✅ 14/14 tests pass over ~650 randomized inputs (fixed seeds) |\n| Binary stdout comparison | N/A — no `add_executable` in CMake, no `[[bin]]` in Cargo.toml |\n| Phase C — every `ERRORS.md` row (8) | ✅ 9/9 tests pass |\n| All feature combinations | ✅ no `[features]` table; default and `--no-default-features` both pass |\n\n## Two harness defects found and fixed (these would have made the suite vacuous)\n\n1. **`cargo test` never rebuilds a `cdylib`.** The first green run was testing a *stale* `libdriver.so`. Proven by mutating `j += 2` → `j += 3`: all 23 tests still passed. Fixed with a mtime staleness assertion in `tests/common/mod.rs` plus `run_tests.sh`, which always builds first.\n2. **Parallel test threads corrupted the captures.** stdout redirection is process-global, so the harness's own `ok` bytes landed inside a capture. Fixed via `.cargo/config.toml` (`RUST_TEST_THREADS=1`) and a hard assert that refuses to run otherwise.\n\nAfter the fixes, two mutants (`j += 3`, `i <= x`) were both killed (7 and 24 failing assertions), confirming the suite has real detection power.\n\n## Notes on the C surface\n\n- Rejection surface is **empty**: `driver` is `void`, contains no `return`/`assert`/null check/range check/enum, and ignores `printf`'s return. `ERRORS.md` documents this and covers the boundary conditions a caller can actually construct (`0`, `-1`, `INT_MIN`, `INT_MIN+1`, randomized negatives, out-of-range enum-like bit patterns, interleaved invalid calls, smallest accepted value).\n- One genuine untestable boundary is documented rather than faked: `j = 2*i` overflows `int` at `x > 1073741823` (signed-overflow UB in C, >10⁹ `printf` calls). The Rust uses `wrapping_add`, matching what the C compiler emits in practice.\n- `c_src/` was not modified; only the gitignored `c_src/build/` directory was created.\n\nArtifacts: `translation/{SYMBOLS.md, ERRORS.md, CONFIGS.md}`, tests in `translation/tests/`, runner `translation/run_tests.sh`."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":578,"cache_read_input_tokens":57639,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":578,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c017869b-fce7-4046-b82f-b5eaf72fb7e7","uuid":"6b3a0bbe-066f-40ba-a0d8-d96eedc2625c","timestamp":"2026-09-05T05:03:59.211Z"}
